# The committed browser bundle. Machine-generated: never merge it textually,
# always rebuild. A textual merge of minified output can silently produce a file
# that parses but is wrong, so -merge forces the conflict to be loud - and the
# correct resolution is ALWAYS "take either side, then npm run build".
#
# `-text eol=lf` is not decorative. core.autocrlf is true on at least one dev
# machine here, and without pinning the bundle to LF a byte-identical rebuild
# would look dirty and fail the freshness gate on line endings alone.
app/build/islands.js  -diff -merge -text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
